{"characterisation":[],"notes":"All 13 tests live in tests/acceptance.part1.test.tsx and use msw (setupServer plus the contract's generated handlers, with my own rows where a criterion says each or all). Run twice: all fail on assertions, none crashes in set-up or rendering. No characterisation tests, because the containers are fixture-only and have nothing of their own to keep.\n\nWording the approved screens do not give is guessed:\n- Inventory form (AC-8.2): fields are found by label patterns (name or ingredient, category, available or quantity, cost, dry matter, energy, storage). Submit is a button named save, add or create. The form opens via the Feed tools menu item \"Add inventory item\".\n- Mapping dialog (AC-3.1): driven with the labels in the approved sample (\"PO line\", \"Lots\", \"Pen assignments\", \"Save mapping\").\n- Conflicts (AC-4.1): the \"Review conflicts\" button is the one on the alert. The review-action check is loose (at least one Resolve mapping / Keep source / review button).\n- AC-2.2 and AC-8.1: values are matched per record within the smallest row or card that holds the record's own name. Numbers are matched ignoring thousands separators. \"Pen ID\" is checked as the returned penName, since the mapping result has no separate pen ID.\n- AC-2.1: the request body is checked for field presence and type, since the mock source adapter's own records are not known to the test.\n- Dates (AC-5.x): accepted as ISO, \"9 Apr\", \"Apr 9\" and numeric forms, all computed from TEST_NOW.\n- Two sessions (AC-1.2): the same screen is rendered, collected and unmounted twice, and the buttons, links and form fields are compared.\nAll 15 tests are in tests/acceptance.part2.test.tsx and render the S-3 container. I ran the file once: all 15 fail, each on an assertion or a failed lookup of the UI the feature will add (e.g. \"Plan feeding\" menu entry, \"Cottonseed hulls\" option, missing returned values). None crash in set-up. `npx tsc --noEmit` is clean. I did not rerun after one small final edit (added a plain-text fallback in `openMenuItem`).\n\nThe S-3 container is still a stub, so the tests guess how the screen is operated. I took the guesses from the approved screens and fixtures; a mismatch would show up as a failed lookup, not as wrong behaviour:\n- **Menus and buttons:** the \"Feed tools\" and \"Feeding entry\" menus, and the submit buttons \"Calculate and save ration\", \"Save feeding plan\" and \"Save actual feeding\".\n- **Form fields:** the approved labels: Ration name, Pen, Selected ration, Per-animal bunk rate, Saved plan, Delivered quantity, Actual feeding time, and the allocation fields. For lot allocations the tests fill per-lot fields if the form has them, otherwise one text box in the \"Lot 14-A: 3,200 lb; ...\" form.\n- **Stock movement form (AC-9.1):** the design has no label for it. The test looks for a button or \"Feed tools\" entry named like \"movement\" and fields labelled item, type and quantity.\n- **Event detail screen:** there is no list-events API call, so the test reads events from the save response. Where a detail button or link exists it clicks it.\n\nHow values are checked:\n- **Number format:** a number matches with or without thousands commas, and a negative needs a minus sign.\n- **Where a value must appear:** it must show in the row, card or list entry named after the pen, lot or ingredient. If the page has no such container, the check falls back to the whole page.\n- **Test data:** it uses pen, lot, ration and ingredient names and numbers the existing fixtures lack, so the fixture content cannot make a test pass.\n- **Wastage ratio:** a forecast `wastageRatio` of 0.065 is expected to show as \"6.5%\" (or \"0.065\").\n\nAC-15.1 covers creating a plan only, not editing one.\nAll 12 tests are in tests/acceptance.part3.test.tsx. They compile (tsc --noEmit clean). Both runs of the file show all 12 failing on assertions or failed lookups, with no set-up or render crashes, against today's placeholder containers, which render the approved sample data and make no API calls. An earlier version of AC-17.1 passed against that sample data, so the feeding quantities were changed to values the sample doesn't contain.\n\nMethod: msw (setupServer) with the generated handlers from lib/api/client.msw.ts. Each test supplies its own rows (a single lot for the metrics and history tests; shuffled weight history for AC-19.1) and keeps a small per-test store, so GET answers follow earlier POST/PUT/void calls.\n\nAssumptions about the UI that the implementation must meet:\n- Screen test containers are rendered with no props: ProcurementLotRecordsContainer (S-2) and FeedManagementContainer (S-3).\n- Label and button wording comes from the approved screens and design fixtures: 'Average animal weight', 'Animals weighed', 'Notes', 'Save weight', 'Edit record', 'Void record' / 'Void selected', 'Feeding entry', 'Adjust future plan', 'Saved plan', 'Delivered quantity (lb)', 'Save actual feeding'; detail labels 'Days on feed', 'Total weight gain', 'Average daily gain', 'Total feed consumed', 'Feed conversion ratio', 'Feed cost / gain'.\n- The weight and feeding tables expose real table rows (tr or role=row) with per-cell text. Row actions are reached through a row checkbox (bulk bar) or a 'More' menu.\n- Edit and feeding-entry forms open in a role=dialog. If a void asks for a reason, it is a textbox named 'reason'; a confirm button named 'Confirm...' or 'Void...' is clicked if present.\n- Dates and numbers are matched format-agnostically (ISO, 'D Mon YYYY', 'Mon D, YYYY'; thousands commas optional).\n- AC-19.1 accepts ascending or descending time order, because the criterion names no direction.\n- AC-17 and AC-20.1 (feeding) and AC-23.1 (feeding) go through the saved-feeding flow because the contract has no endpoint that lists feeding events. AC-20.1 covers a weight edit and a feeding void; AC-23.1 covers a weight save and a feeding save.\n- AC-22.3: the API has no field for non-feed costs, so the test proves the displayed basis ('recorded feed costs') and the returned feed-cost-per-gain value, not the calculation itself.\nAll 13 tests are in tests/acceptance.part4.test.tsx. They type-check, and all 13 fail today on assertions, not crashes. The S-1 and S-4 containers are still stubs that render the static design fixtures, so the data my tests supply never appears. I ran the file twice, so I have no further runs.\n\nJudgement calls and risks:\n- **Test data.** Each test supplies its own data through msw handlers with the contract's response shapes. Report rows are filtered by the request's query params, so each filter change has to produce a different result set.\n- **Number formats.** Most value checks are substring matches on the page text. Money and tonnage allow an alternative format, such as /2,?318/ or /11,?000|5\\.5/.\n- **Filter widgets.** Filters are driven through the approved fields: the Sex radio, the Breed select, the Lot and Pen comboboxes, and \"Apply filters\". I did not drive date-range changes through the calendar popover, which is too fragile in jsdom. The tests check that the dateFrom and dateTo sent match what the Date range control shows.\n- **AC-24.1.** Best and worst lots are identified by a \"best\" marker and a \"lowest\" or \"worst\" marker on the lot row. The lot data is built so one lot is best and one worst on every metric.\n- **Export (AC-27.x).** The generated client calls JSON.parse on the CSV body, so it cannot download raw CSV. The tests therefore accept any delivery route: a request to the export endpoint, an anchor click, window.open, or nav. Whichever route is used, the URL must be export.csv or export.pdf and must carry the scope: sex, breed, and the dateFrom and dateTo of the last displayed report, with no lotId or penId. If a Blob is produced, its text must contain the rows and scope. The \"CSV/PDF report exported for the selected scope.\" toast must also appear.\n- **AC-29.1 (the riskiest).** The AC names no screen. I read it as the S-1 overview, since S-1 is the one approved screen that lists REQ-29 for lots and pens. The test needs all seven record kinds on that screen: procurement vendor \"Prairie Cattle Co.\", lots, pens, inventory \"Soybean meal\", ration \"North Yard Grower\", feeding \"Pen 14\", and a weight of 1,246. Procurement, inventory, ration, feeding and weight come from the default contract examples of the other endpoints, not from the overview response, so S-1 would have to load those endpoints too.\n- **AC-29.2.** The test uses the contract's eight project-brief sections. It expects each title to be shown and each body to be reachable, by clicking the title if it is collapsed.","probes":[],"tests":[{"acId":"AC-1.1","file":"tests/acceptance.part1.test.tsx","name":"AC_1_1_ShowsSharedWorkspaceWithoutSignInOrRoleSelector","screen":"S-1"},{"acId":"AC-1.2","file":"tests/acceptance.part1.test.tsx","name":"AC_1_2_ShowsSameControlsInTwoSessions","screen":"S-1"},{"acId":"AC-2.1","file":"tests/acceptance.part1.test.tsx","name":"AC_2_1_SyncRequestCarriesPoLineVendorCostHeadWeightBreedAgeSource","screen":"S-2"},{"acId":"AC-2.2","file":"tests/acceptance.part1.test.tsx","name":"AC_2_2_ShowsReturnedVendorCostHeadWeightBreedAgeSource","screen":"S-2"},{"acId":"AC-3.1","file":"tests/acceptance.part1.test.tsx","name":"AC_3_1_ShowsPoLineToLotToPenAssociationForSingleLot","screen":"S-2"},{"acId":"AC-3.1","file":"tests/acceptance.part1.test.tsx","name":"AC_3_1_ShowsEachAssociationWhenPoLineSplitAcrossLots","screen":"S-2"},{"acId":"AC-4.1","file":"tests/acceptance.part1.test.tsx","name":"AC_4_1_ShowsEachConflictWithStatusExistingMappingAndReviewAction","screen":"S-2"},{"acId":"AC-5.1","file":"tests/acceptance.part1.test.tsx","name":"AC_5_1_ShowsReturnedTargetWeightAndProjectedDate","screen":"S-2"},{"acId":"AC-5.2","file":"tests/acceptance.part1.test.tsx","name":"AC_5_2_ProjectedDateEmptyForZeroOrNegativeAdg","screen":"S-2"},{"acId":"AC-6.1","file":"tests/acceptance